# 4 Carat Radiant Cut Diamond Ring: The $80K vs $7.9K Truth

A 4 carat radiant cut diamond ring is not a subtle purchase. The face-up size is approximately 10.0×7.7mm for an elongated stone — the first weight in the radiant series where the stone crosses 10mm in face-up length. You see it before you see the hand wearing it.

In current certified market inventory, lab 4ct radiant rings start at [$7,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Natural 4ct radiant rings start at [$80,372](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

That gap is 10.2×. It is the widest lab-to-natural spread in the entire radiant weight series — and it only exists because natural 4ct radiant stones are genuinely rare.

**TL;DR:**
- → **The 10.2× Gap:** lab 4ct radiant ring at [$7,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), natural entry at [$80,372](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — the widest gap in the radiant series
- → **Best lab pick:** [4.00ct D-VVS1 IGI $7,031](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$7,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — D-VVS1 IGI, 10mm face-up
- → **Natural entry:** [4.01ct D-VS2 GIA $79,512](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$80,372](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — GIA certified, D-VS2
- → **Natural sweet spot:** [4.01ct F-VVS1 GIA $109,801](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27292860?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [$860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **[$110,661](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27292860?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — F-VVS1, GIA certified
- 4ct radiant face-up: ~10.0×7.7mm. Crosses [The 10mm Statement](#the-10mm-statement) — visible from across a room
- The half-carat upgrade from 3.5ct costs [$28,531](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more in natural. [$1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more in lab. Same stone. [The 10× Wall](#the-10-wall) explains why
- See the [radiant cut engagement rings pillar](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) for the full shape guide

