## The 10× Wall

The 10× Wall is the price barrier that appears at 4ct in natural radiant diamonds. It is not just the lab-to-natural gap — it is a simultaneous shift in natural per-carat pricing that makes 4ct feel like a different market entirely.

At 3.5ct, the natural radiant entry is approximately [$14,484 per carat](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=3.4-3.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). At 4ct, the natural entry is approximately [$19,828 per carat](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=3.8-4.3&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). That is a [$28,531](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) jump for half a carat more.

You are not just paying for more weight. You are paying for significantly rarer stones at a significantly higher per-carat rate. That is The 10× Wall.

For lab buyers, The 10× Wall does not exist. The lab 4ct D-VVS1 ring at [$7,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is just [$1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more than the [3.5ct lab ring at $6,711](/3-5-carat-radiant-cut-diamond-ring). Lab is not subject to natural scarcity pricing.

At 4ct, that gap is the clearest case for lab over natural anywhere in the radiant series.

For natural buyers, you need to decide whether you are paying for rarity or for size. Both matter — but they cost very different amounts at this weight.

[![4 carat radiant cut diamond solitaire engagement ring in yellow gold](/images/radiant-cut-solitaire-engagement-ring-yellow-gold.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=3.8-4.3&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

## 4ct Radiant Cut Lab Diamond Prices

Lab 4ct radiant stones are IGI-certified and chemically identical to natural diamonds. They are not subject to any scarcity premium — which is why natural stones cost [$80,000+](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and lab stones do not. All rings below use the [Ten Prong Solitaire 14K White Gold (item 311235)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at [$860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

