## Expert Summary

A 4 carat radiant cut diamond ring crosses [The 10mm Statement](#the-10mm-statement) — the face-up milestone where a radiant becomes clearly visible from across a room in normal indoor lighting. Both lab and natural stones deliver this at 4ct. The decision between them is not a quality decision — it is a values decision.

Lab at [$7,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) complete is the best face-up-per-dollar in the entire [radiant cut engagement rings](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) series. The half-carat upgrade from 3.5ct costs just [$1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in lab — always take it. That is a visible upgrade for a price difference most people spend without thinking.

Natural at [$80,372](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/18152689?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) entry is where you hit [The 10× Wall](#the-10-wall). The per-carat price jumps from ~[$14,484/ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=3.4-3.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at 3.5ct to ~[$19,828/ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=3.8-4.3&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at 4ct. The [F-VVS1 GIA at $110,661](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27292860?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the strongest natural pick at this weight — F color, VVS1 clarity, GIA certified, with excellent resale positioning.

Both stones look identical from across the room. At 4ct, that is the core question every buyer has to face and answer for themselves.

